16\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"  These fixes were accepted because data races are bugs, not \\\"concurrency mechanisms left to users.\\\"\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## The Race Is Real and Reproducible\\n\\n  From issue #4588:\\n\\n  WARNING: DATA RACE\\n\\n  Write at 0x... by goroutine X:\\n\\n    [defer in Middleware]\\n\\n  Read at 0x... by goroutine Y:\\n\\n    [user handler accessing context]\\n\\n  This is undefined behavior. The Go memory model states: \\\"Programs that modify data being simultaneously accessed by multiple goroutines must serialize such access.\\\"\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## The Fix is Correct\\n\\n  The fix simply removes dead code:\\n\\n```go\\n\\n  // Before: Save and restore (unnecessary)\\n\\n  savedCtx := c.Request.Context()\\n\\n  defer func() { c.Request = c.Request.WithContext(savedCtx) }()\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"these fix were accept becaus data race are bug not concurr mechan left to user sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file label mileston the race is real and reproduc from issu 4588 warn data race write at 0x by goroutin x defer in middlewar read at 0x by goroutin y user handler access context this is undefin behavior the go memori model state program that modifi data be simultan access by multipl goroutin must serial such access sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file label mileston the fix is correct the fix simpli remov dead code go befor save and restor unnecessari savedctx c request context defer func c request c request withcontext savedctx\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"b40b58fd0d2fea42\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.28222840838553415, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.07828588340790599, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7580943, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:16\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## The Defer Provides No Benefit\\n\\nLet's analyze what the current code does:\\n\\n```go\\n\\n  savedCtx := c.Request.Context()\\n\\n  defer func() {\\n\\n      c.Request = c.Request.WithContext(savedCtx)  // ← Restores AFTER request completes\\n\\n  }()\\n\\n  ctx := cfg.Propagators.Extract(savedCtx, propagation.HeaderCarrier(c.Request.Header))\\n\\n  // ...\\n\\n  c.Request = c.Request.WithContext(ctx)  // ← Sets new context\\n\\n  c.Next()  // ← Processes request\\n\\n  // When we return, defer runs and \\\"restores\\\" the old context\\n\\n```\\n\\n  Question: Why restore the context after the request is complete?\\n\\n  - After c.Next() returns, the request has been fully processed\\n\\n  - Gin doesn't reuse *gin.Context instances across requests\\n\\n  - Downstream handlers may spawn goroutines that read c.Request.Context()\\n\\n  - The deferred write to c.Request races with those goroutine reads\\n\\n  - There is no code that benefits from this restoration\\n\\n**Source ID**: [SRC-PR-07]\\n\\n# Pull Request: otelgin: remove unneeded context save/restore to avoid data race (open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib#8014)\\n\\n**Canonical URL**: https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-go-contrib/pull/8014  \\n\\n**Author**: nicksherron  \\n\\n**Created**: 2025-10-14T04:01:24Z · **Updated**: 2025-10-17T10:42:07Z  \\n\\n**Collected**: 2026-07-14T14:35:41Z  \\n\\n**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## The Performance Argument is Backwards\\n\\nThe current code with the defer is slower than the fix:\\n\\n  Current code overhead:\\n\\n  - Allocates closure for defer\\n\\n  - Saves context reference\\n\\n  - Executes deferred function on return\\n\\n  - Calls WithContext() twice (once to set, once to \\\"restore\\\")\\n\\n  Fixed code:\\n\\n  - No defer\\n\\n  - No closure allocation\\n\\n  - One fewer WithContext() call\\n\\n  - No unnecessary context copy\\n\\n Benchmark comparison (removing defer should show improvement):\\n\\n  -  Current: ~3 allocations per request\\n\\n  -  Fixed:   ~2 allocations per request\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"label mileston the defer provid no benefit let s analyz what the current code doe go savedctx c request context defer func c request c request withcontext savedctx restor after request complet ctx cfg propag extract savedctx propag headercarri c request header c request c request withcontext ctx set new context c next process request when we return defer run and restor the old context question whi restor the context after the request is complet after c next return the request ha been fulli process gin doesn t reus gin context instanc across request downstream handler may spawn goroutin that read c request context the defer write to c request race with those goroutin read there is no code that benefit from this restor sourc id src pr 07 pull request otelgin remov unneed context save restor to avoid data race open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib 8014 canon url http github com open telemetri opentelemetri go contrib pull 8014 author nicksherron creat 2025 10 14t04 01 24z updat 2025 10 17t10 42 07z collect 2026 07 14t14 35 41z state close branch fix otelgin data race main chang 83 10 across 2 file label mileston the perform argument is backward the current code with the defer is slower than the fix current code overhead alloc closur for defer save context refer execut defer function on return call withcontext twice onc to set onc to restor fix code no defer no closur alloc one fewer withcontext call no unnecessari context copi benchmark comparison remov defer should show improv current 3 alloc per request fix 2 alloc per request\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"id\": \"0e4329537c0aa36a\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2767573083855342, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.07828588340790599, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7398573, \"dataset_name\": \"C2Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"8753acb88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"location\": \"opentelemetry/pulls/opentelemetry-go-contrib-8014.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 33019, \"chunk_count\": 21, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:53:51\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:10:16\", \"token_count\": 10517, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"74f29ea88a9c11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**State**: closed  \\n\\n**Branch**: `fix/otelgin-data-race` → `main`  \\n\\n**Changes**: +83 / -10 across 2 files  \\n\\n**Labels**: —  \\n\\n**Milestone**: —\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Timeline\\n\\n- 2025-10-14T04:05:44Z · **ready_for_review** by nicksherron\\n\\n- 2025-10-14T04:05:44Z · **review_requested** by nicksherron\\n\\n- 2025-10-14T04:05:44Z · **review_requested** by nicksherron\\n\\n- 2025-10-14T04:05:53Z · **review_requested** by github-actions[bot]\\n\\n- 2025-10-17T10:41:5