{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"PR #8014 was closed because the OpenTelemetry Go SIG decided that removing the deferred context restoration would be semantically incorrect.\n\nThe restoration intentionally removes the otelgin span once the middleware returns, so a parent middleware’s post-`c.Next()` work does not create spans as children of a trace that has already finished. Maintainers considered that established behavior—also present in other instrumentations—correct. They concluded that callers launching goroutines should explicitly pass the needed context/span instead. Damien Mathieu closed the PR after the SIG discussion on October 16. [SRC-PR-07] [SRC-NOTE-04]"}}
